WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.601
-Hey, guys. We're hanging out
with Jon Hamm right here.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:04.868
Now...

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:09.901
I know we were saying earlier,
you -- you were in a musical,

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.334
but you were never in a band.

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:12.968
-I mean, it's, like,
not entirely true.

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.734
-Yeah, a lot of people
don't know this,

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:17.267
but before our careers took off,
we were both in a --

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.467
-I just didn't want to brag.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.901
-Well, we were both
in a band together.

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:24.200
-Yeah. I mean, I know. It's --
I should have brought it.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.834
I should have brought this.
-What?

00:00:25.834 --> 00:00:28.167
-I found one of our old touring
T-shirts the other day.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.467
We were in a band called Burlap.
-Burlap.

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:32.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.267
Burlap.
We were sort of, like,

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.167
an outlaw, country,
rock 'n' roll.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.501
-Rock 'n' roll. Yeah, country.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.667
-Yeah, but looking back,
I think we might have focused

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.701
a little too much on our image.

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:43.267
-No, no. It was a good look.
It was the right look.

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:45.834
I just feel like
that the songwriting

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.434
really needed a little work.
-Right.

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:50.200
People would come to our shows
based off of our look

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.400
and they expected to hear songs
about trucks and trains

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.968
and love gone wrong.

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.834
-Mamas and...
-Mamas. Yeah.

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:59.501
-But we did not write songs
about any of that.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.300
-Not at all. No, we did not.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.434
Well, you're not
gonna believe this.

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:07.267
-No.
Don't tell me you have a clip.

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.334
-[ Laughter ]
-I have a clip.

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:12.234
Here's the very first
performance of Jon Hamm and I

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:14.501
in our old band, Burlap.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:23.934
Tractorfest '99!
How y'all doing tonight?!

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:25.200
-Whoo!

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.300
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.234
We are Burlap!

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:31.300
And just like the fabric,

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.701
we are rough, rugged,
and itchy as heck.

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:37.067
-Country style!

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:39.634
I see a lot of outlaws
in the crowd tonight.

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:42.767
What do you say we rock
this house across state lines?

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.834
-Ha ha!
I think we got just the song

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.934
to keep Smokey off our tail.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:48.701
Hit it!

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:52.501
-One, a-two.
A-one, two, three.

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:55.000
-♪ I love, I love my lollipop ♪

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.601
♪ I love my lollipop,
I love my lollipop ♪

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:01.200
♪ I love, I love my lollipop ♪

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.767
♪ I love my lollipop girls ♪

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.000
-Thank you.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.501
[ Audience jeering ]

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:08.701
-Oh, no. That's not...

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:10.701
Hey!
-Hey! Come on!

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:14.934
-I got to say...

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:18.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:22.334
I-I will say, that holds up
a lot better than I remember.

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:23.868
-Yeah, yeah.
-It wasn't bad.

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:25.767
-Yeah, it certainly
went a lot better

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:28.133
than our performance
at Bootscoot '99.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:30.467
-Oh, Bootscoot. Guh!
A disaster!

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:32.734
I'm really glad
you don't have a clip of that.

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:35.133
-Well...
-No way!

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:38.667
-Let's look at another clip of
me and Jon's old band, Burlap.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:42.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:45.400
-Alright!

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.334
Bootscoot '99,
let's hear some noise!

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.501
-Ohh!

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:50.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:53.801
In case our reputation
does not precede us,

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:55.200
we are Burlap,

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.667
and we're basically
musical chicken wire!

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:59.100
-Yes, sir!

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.334
It looks like we got us a lot
of rascals out here tonight.

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:04.367
But what do you say
we wrestle these varmints up?

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:06.434
-Country style!

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:09.934
-A-one, a-two.
A-one, two, three.

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:12.601
-♪ DVD collectors ♪

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:15.734
♪ We're DVD collectors ♪

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:19.267
♪ Like videotapes but on CD ♪

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:22.133
♪ We like collecting DVDs ♪

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:24.968
-♪ There's a lot to enjoy
about DVDs ♪

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:28.334
♪ Like bonus content
and commentaries ♪

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:31.434
-♪ Scene selection,
animated menus ♪

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:34.734
♪ The last DVD I bought
was "Meet Joe Black" ♪

00:03:34.734 --> 00:03:37.200
-♪ DVD collectors ♪

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.434
♪ We're DVD collectors ♪

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:43.934
♪ We like videotapes but on CD ♪

00:03:43.934 --> 00:03:46.501
♪ We like collecting DVDs ♪

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:48.667
-♪ Baby ♪
-♪ Baby ♪

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:50.501
-That's right!
-Oh, come on.

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:51.767
[ Audience jeering ]

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:54.033
-Come on, now!
-Stop it!

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.334
[ Audience jeering ]

00:03:56.334 --> 00:03:58.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:01.467
-Wow!
That was a crazy, intense show.

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:03.501
-It was.
-Yeah.

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:05.501
Uh, that was intense.

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:07.200
That was very intense,
very intense.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:11.634
-Yeah, that was not
as intense as our --

00:04:11.634 --> 00:04:13.667
as our --

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:16.033
It was not as intense
as our farewell.

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:18.501
-Our farewell --
Our third show.

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:20.234
-Well, yeah. Of course.

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:22.167
I'm talking about
Rustbucket '99.

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:24.234
-Oh, Rustbucket.
-Let's take a look.

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:25.701
The third and final
performance ever...

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:27.300
-[ Sighs ]

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.434
-[ Laughter ]
-...by Burlap.

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:30.834
Here we go.

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:32.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.934
Rustbucket '99!
Let's get rowdy!

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:39.634
-Whoo!

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:41.734
-Now, just in case
you didn't read

00:04:41.734 --> 00:04:43.200
your commemorative
festival program,

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.167
we are Burlap, and our
tour bus is a wheelbarrow.

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.634
-Heh! Country style!

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:51.334
-Oh, man, you know,
you're always saying that,

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:52.667
but why don't you tell them

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:54.567
what "country style"
really means?

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:59.133
-Well, take a Little rock,
a little roll, a little rebel,

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:02.033
and a little rear tire damage,

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:03.968
then you smother that thang
in gravy.

00:05:03.968 --> 00:05:05.400
-Oh, hit it!

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.467
-A-one, two.
A-one, two, three.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:11.567
-♪ Java in my cup,
time to drink it up ♪

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:14.801
♪ Gotta have my coffee
or I get real grouchy ♪

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:17.801
♪ Grinding up the beans
just a splash of cream ♪

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:20.901
♪ Gotta have my coffee,
or I turn into a grump ♪

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:23.834
-♪ Americano, macchiato,
cappuccino, latte ♪

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:26.934
-♪ We don't give a hoot
if you like it or not-te ♪

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:29.601
-♪ Slide-whistle break ♪

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:32.501
♪♪

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:34.667
[ Slide whistles blowing ]

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:38.534
♪♪

00:05:38.534 --> 00:05:41.400
-♪ Now I slide your whistle,
you slide mine ♪

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.834
[ Slide whistles blowing ]

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:48.167
♪♪

00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:50.300
Hey, come on, now!
Hey! Get off me!

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.234
-That's enough! That's enough!

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:53.701
[ Audience jeering ]

00:05:53.701 --> 00:05:56.067
We're outta here! We try to do
something fun, and you guys...

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:59.234
[ Audience jeering ]

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:01.467
-Well...
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:04.234
At least we went out on top.

00:06:04.234 --> 00:06:07.033
-On top.
-My thanks to Jon Hamm!

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.968
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.100
Stick around, everybody.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:12.467
-Whoo!

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:16.467
♪♪

